# dependencies
node_modules/

# build output
dist/
site/.astro/

# Cloudflare Workers
.wrangler/

# env / secrets — never commit real keys
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
*.log

# Local dev-preview tooling config (machine-specific paths)
.claude/

# Raw photo dump (~1GB of originals) — working set lives in design/photos/
photos-for-design/

# Generated review sheet — rebuild with design/review-photos.py
design/photo-placement.jpg

# Design build outputs (regenerate with design/build.py)
design/*.dc.html
design/your-church-site-design.html
design/preview/
design/people-at-front.jpg

# Fairhaven Kids source photography — the pastor's originals, ~450MB of full-resolution
# candid shots of identifiable children. Deliberately NOT tracked:
#
#   1. The standing rule in handoff/BRIEF-kids.md §3 is that no member data
#      goes in the repo, ever. Photographs of children are the sharpest version
#      of that rule, not an exception to it.
#   2. Git history is permanent. A 450MB mistake here cannot be undone by a
#      later commit, only by rewriting history for everyone.
#
# The DERIVED background — downscaled, duotoned, faces no longer the subject —
# is committed under app/public/. The originals stay on the pastor's machine.
handoff/kids-design/Candid Kids Photos/

# The Fairhaven Kids print artwork too. "door hanger" and the invite-card mockups carry
# Joanna Sutter's name and personal mobile number in the artwork itself — the
# same class of thing as the real phone number that once had to be scrubbed out
# of a schema comment. Public on a printed card is not the same as public in a
# git history that is cloned, mirrored and permanent.
handoff/kids-design/

# One transcript-cleaning run at a time — local state, not content
site/transcripts/.cleaning.lock
